# MCSP Reconciliation 0.22

Status: Constructive reconciliation checkpoint
Qualification: Under Conditional Experiment
Lineage: 0.13 through 0.21

## Purpose

Reconcile the current MCSP kernel, semantic architecture, hardware-clearance method, hardware-independence target, and qualification work without silently rewriting originating versions.

Earlier files remain historical evidence.

## 1. Current kernel candidate

The smallest current pre-semantic kernel candidate is:

    DETERMINATE CONDITION

It SHALL NOT intrinsically require:

    object
    name
    identity
    value
    state
    Boolean
    position
    order
    taxonomy
    topology
    ISA
    assembler
    ABI
    operating system
    device class
    physical encoding

CONDITION and DETERMINATION are not treated as two independent kernel objects.

Determinacy is the aspect by which a condition can constrain later interpretation enough to reject arbitrary semantic projection.

## 2. Corrected status of earlier candidates

STATE:
    derived semantic construct; not kernel.

DISTINGUISH:
    first-order semantic/qualification operation candidate; not currently kernel.

RELATION:
    semantic structural substrate candidate; not proven kernel primitive.

IDENTITY / POSITION / ORDER / SCOPE:
    irreducible semantic-role candidates from earlier reduction;
    not pre-semantic kernel primitives.

BOUNDARY:
    established by interpretation/applicability; not currently kernel.

INTERPRETATION:
    semantic commencement operation; not currently kernel ontology.

POSTURE / GESTURE:
    explanatory/decomposition views; not kernel primitives.

TRANSFER:
    useful canonical candidate; explicitly non-primitive pending decomposition.

